#: ../../../source/user_guide/remote_execution.rst:94
msgid ""
"Multiple knobs control multi-machine behaviour, and they are deliberately"
" separate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/remote_execution.rst:96
msgid "``cpus_per_job``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/remote_execution.rst:97
msgid "The number of cores each job is given."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/remote_execution.rst:99
msgid "``max_concurrent``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/remote_execution.rst:100
msgid ""
"How many jobs run on a machine **at once**.  Enforced during execution by"
" a per-host semaphore, so a batch can send two concurrent jobs to one "
"machine and one to another."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/remote_execution.rst:104
msgid ""
"When ``max_concurrent`` is not given it is derived from ``cpus_total``, "
"``cpus_per_job`` and ``license_tokens``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/remote_execution.rst:106
msgid "``weight``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/remote_execution.rst:107
msgid ""
"What **share of the batch** a machine receives.  Applied when jobs are "
"assigned.  Defaults to the machine's concurrency capacity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/remote_execution.rst:109
msgid "``cpus_total`` (Optional)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/remote_execution.rst:110
msgid ""
"Total cores on the machine. If leaft unset, it is measured once over SSH "
"before any job is dispatched. Setting it explicitly skips that probe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/remote_execution.rst:113
msgid ""
"If ``cpus_per_job`` * ``max_concurrent`` exceeds ``cpus_total``, a "
"**over-subscription Warning** will be given but preceeding to solver."
msgstr ""

